# Changelog – Pencil Snake vs Monster Eraser (Extreme Edition)

## Overview

This release transforms the original **Pencil Snake vs Monster Eraser** into a more polished, responsive, and production-ready web game. The update introduces new gameplay mechanics, improved visuals, enhanced audio, better mobile support, and comprehensive stability improvements while maintaining compatibility with GitHub Pages.

---

## ✨ New Features

### Adaptive Difficulty & Dynamic Win Targets

The victory requirement now scales automatically based on the selected difficulty level.

| Difficulty       | Target Score |
| ---------------- | -----------: |
| Easy             |    40 Points |
| Medium (Default) |    60 Points |
| Hard             |    80 Points |
| Super            |   100 Points |

This provides a balanced progression and a more engaging experience across all difficulty levels.

---

### Procedural Audio Engine

Implemented a real-time audio system using the **Web Audio API**, removing the dependency on external sound files.

Generated sound effects include:

* Point collection effects
* Sharpener Power activation
* Victory fanfare
* Game Over effects
* Countdown timer beeps

All sounds are synthesized directly in the browser, improving reliability and loading performance.

---

### Light & Dark Themes

Added two fully supported visual themes.

#### Sketchbook Theme

* Warm ivory background
* Charcoal-style graphics
* Classic notebook appearance

#### Chalkboard Theme

* Dark slate background
* Neon glowing visuals
* Enhanced contrast for low-light environments

Theme switching updates the entire interface, including:

* Game canvas
* UI controls
* Buttons
* Modal dialogs
* 3D scene lighting

---

### Interactive 3D Main Menu

Integrated a dynamic **Three.js** powered background featuring:

* Rotating graphite pencil
* Floating classic pink eraser
* Orbiting pencil shavings
* Mouse and touch parallax effects
* Smooth animations with dynamic lighting

The result is a more immersive and modern main menu experience.

---

## 🛠 Bug Fixes & Improvements

### Safe Spawn System

Prevented immediate player elimination by introducing a protected spawn area.

Improvements include:

* Safe starting path
* Controlled obstacle generation
* Fair gameplay initialization

---

### Responsive Canvas

Resolved layout issues affecting different screen sizes.

Fixes include:

* Correct aspect ratio calculations
* Improved canvas scaling
* Fixed mobile boundary collisions
* Enhanced responsiveness across devices

---

### Responsive Modals

Refactored all modal components for better usability.

Updated:

* Start Modal
* Victory Modal
* Game Over Modal

Additional improvements:

* Moved modal containers outside the canvas wrapper
* Implemented `100dvh` viewport sizing
* Prevented mobile browser UI clipping
* Eliminated unwanted scrolling

---

### GitHub Pages Compatibility

Improved deployment stability for static hosting.

#### Offline Prompt Library

Added **30+ built-in creative drawing prompts**.

If no Gemini API key is provided, the game automatically switches to offline prompts without interrupting gameplay.

#### WebGL Fallback Protection

Added graceful fallback handling for browsers or devices without WebGL support.

If hardware acceleration is unavailable:

* The 3D menu is automatically disabled.
* The core 2D game remains fully playable.
* Runtime errors are prevented through fallback logic.

